{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-80146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-80146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =3+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =12 \\\\ R & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{60}^{∘})\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-80146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ac5871d7d37c9a8e9118aede4ce35e63e9f4c1e2d1bef300ada95081de99cd9"} {"question" "q-80146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-80146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{60}^{∘})"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘})"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{60}^{∘})"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘})"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{60}^{∘})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-80146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{60}^{∘})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-107568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-107568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-107568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ac5871d7d37c9a8e9118aede4ce35e63e9f4c1e2d1bef300ada95081de99cd9"} {"question" "q-107568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-107568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2\\sqrt{3})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})"] ["math" "{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "{60}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-107568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-274595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ in the form $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Use the **exact value** for $R,$ and round $ϕ$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-274595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\ ϕ & ≈1.292\\,\\text{rad},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(ϕ)+{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡(ϕ) & ={7}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡(ϕ)+{cos}^{2}⁡(ϕ)) & =49+4 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =53 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{53}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)≈\\sqrt{53}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1.292)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-274595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ac5871d7d37c9a8e9118aede4ce35e63e9f4c1e2d1bef300ada95081de99cd9"} {"question" "q-274595" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-274595" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{53}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-274595" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-274595" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.292"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-328001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ in the form $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,{90}^{∘}).$\n\n$-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$\n {{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘})$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-328001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{3}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\  & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={3}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =9+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =18 \\\\ R & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{45}^{∘})\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-328001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ac5871d7d37c9a8e9118aede4ce35e63e9f4c1e2d1bef300ada95081de99cd9"} {"question" "q-328001" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-328001" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-328001" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-328001" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "45"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-328007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+ϕ)$ with $0<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0,$ what is the value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-328007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for cosine gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ ϕ & =arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\ ϕ & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-328007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ac5871d7d37c9a8e9118aede4ce35e63e9f4c1e2d1bef300ada95081de99cd9"} {"question" "q-328007" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"} {"question" "q-328007" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14053852/state.json" "file_sha256" "c356ebc93db47aef83660852d0cfe121bbc642d1c606da83115b3e71fd0b99b0"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1810 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
